spec mg05-gapless-sequence-unique: 2 sessions, 20 permutations
# MG05, UNIQUE on n. A gapless per-year sequence: each transaction reads max(n)
# for 2026 and creates max + 1. Without a constraint both read 1 and both create 2:
# write skew, permitted under snapshot isolation (F1). With UNIQUE on (:Inv).n the
# second CREATE is a ConstraintViolation and the sequence stays gapless.

starting permutation: s1r s1w s1c s2r s2w s2c
step s1r: MATCH (i:Inv {y:2026}) RETURN max(i.n) AS m
m
-
1
(1 row)
step s1w: MATCH (i:Inv {y:2026}) WITH max(i.n) AS m CREATE (j:Inv {y:2026, n:m + 1}) RETURN j.n AS n
n
-
2
(1 row)
step s1c: COMMIT
step s2r: MATCH (i:Inv {y:2026}) RETURN max(i.n) AS m
m
-
1
(1 row)
step s2w: MATCH (i:Inv {y:2026}) WITH max(i.n) AS m CREATE (j:Inv {y:2026, n:m + 1}) RETURN j.n AS n
ERROR: exec: constraint violation: UNIQUE constraint on (Inv).n: value 2 already exists
step s2c: COMMIT
ERROR: cypher: transaction poisoned by a prior failed Exec statement — call Rollback
final final: MATCH (i:Inv {y:2026}) RETURN i.n AS n ORDER BY n
n
-
1
2
(2 rows)

